## Summary

**iter-142 — LLM-TPS consistency check (7th diversity-check instance)**

Landed the signposted 7th instance of the session-summary diversity-check pattern, targeting `llm_tps` (LLM stream throughput, iter-052). A sustained slow LLM stream starves the TTS worker no matter how fast STT/TTS run — there was a per-turn print and a median line but no sustained-run sentinel.

What's notable: this is the **first inverted-direction continuous bucketer**. The three prior continuous instances (sentence-length, stt-rtf, tts-rtf) all had a *low* "fine" value; `llm_tps` is bigger-is-better, so `_llm_tps_bucket` puts the fine state (`"fast"`, ≥25 tps) at the *high* end and flips the boundaries. The inversion lives entirely in the bucketer boundaries and the filter's excluded-set — `_longest_consecutive_run` and the emit machinery are untouched, confirming the run-scan primitive is genuinely direction-agnostic.

- `examples/_chat_metrics.py`: `_llm_tps_bucket` + `_emit_llm_tps_consistency_line`, wired into `print_session_summary`.
- `GENO.md`: updated atomically (six→seven instances + filter-rule/continuous-metric/threshold bullets).
- Tests: new `test_emit_llm_tps_consistency_line.py` (+21), doc-sync test extended.

**Verification:** unit `1674 passed` (1653 prior + 21 new); integration `30 passed, 1 skipped`. FF-merged to main (`f274aad`), log committed (`a043e05`), worktree removed.

